animation-duration: a duration-list longhand, read as animation-delay is. 'auto' (the initial value) keeps the
durations the animation list declares; a declared list replaces them item by item; a negative duration is invalid.
The PAL follows each animation shorthand with the longhand's 'auto', as a CSS shorthand resets its longhands.
CSS Animations 1: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-animations-1/#animation-duration

